# Platform backends

Core depends on **traits** (names illustrative): host metrics, storage
discovery, process supervision, credential store, optional OS image ops.
Platform crates implement those traits.

## Hard rules

1. Prefer **one Jetson-family backend** with runtime capability detection over
   separate Orin vs A-box business trees unless hardware forces a feature flag.
2. Mac/dev backends may stub metrics/storage — still satisfy trait contracts
   for day-one tests.
3. Selecting a backend is build/feature/`--target` concern — not scattered
   conditionals in reconcile code.

